Package: mixRSMflow
Type: Package
Title: Integrated Design, Modeling, Optimization and Visualization for Mixture Experiments
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Walter Esfrain", "Pereira", email = "walterufpb@yahoo.com.br", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Magali Haidee Pereira", "Martinez", role = "aut")
    )
Description: Provides an integrated workflow for the design, analysis, diagnosis,
    interpretation, optimization, uncertainty quantification, and visualization
    of mixture experiments. The core includes simplex and constrained designs,
    Scheffe and alternative blending models, mixture-process workflows, optimal
    designs, prediction-variance diagnostics, multiresponse optimization,
    optimum-location uncertainty, static vector graphics, and optional
    interactive, mixed-effects, Bayesian, Gaussian-process, and Shiny backends.
    The package emphasizes explicit mixture constraints, auditable decisions,
    numerical diagnostics, and reproducible teaching and scientific workflows.
